    expression, a return, an if or a for), without imports, annotations, declarations
    without code and constants, plus one per entry of a data file. The jar has 31 such
    statements in its Java code and 1 language entry. 11 of the 31 achieve the same result
    as a statement of Draconic Evolution or Brandon's Core: the block properties chain of
    OpaqueMachineProperties, the null check of the crystal part offset, the damage of
    Float.MAX_VALUE / 100 in four handlers, the Draconic tech level, the water animal check,
    the claim.xp label key and the two statements of the F1 check. That is 11 of 32, or 34
    percent. The other 20 statements and the language entry, whose English text is this
    mod's own, do not reproduce upstream code. The Draconium Chest fix in particular works
    in another way than upstream's: the menu remembers the grid that its result came from
    and computes the result again before a click when the grid has changed since.
